{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382975-humanity-variant-the-beast","id":1382975,"title":"Humanity variant - The Beast","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-21T08:33:13-07:00","id":1382975,"title":"Humanity variant - The Beast","content":"Putting some thoughts to a reworking of Humanity that would accommodate Paths and such within the current V5 system. What if we measure how strong the Beast is within you, not how much Humanity you retain. The higher your rating, the stronger the Beast has become. The lower the rating, the better you can interact with humans and relate to them. This would take the current systems of abilities based on Humanity score and reverse it.<br /> <br /> As you go through unlife, the Beast would gain victories (stains). When the Beast has accumulated more victories than its current rating, the vampire risk Degeneration. They can choose to be impaired for the remainder of the session or allow the Beast to gain a stronger hold, increasing their Beast rating by one and dropping the victories to 0. <br /> <br /> I think this system might better reflect a goal of having Paths, as they were always a way to keep the Beast at bay. Additionally, with some of the Loresheets we have seen, they simply get reworded to say that the Beast gains no victories for certain actions you can undertake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24641-sarcasticjazzhands","name":"SarcasticJazzHands","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T16:07:10-07:00","id":1383047,"title":"","content":"This is a great idea... but I'm partial.<br /> <br /> In my homebrew rules characters have both a Humanity score *and* a Beast score. You could thus have someone with a very high Beast AND a very high humanity -- someone who is easily overwhelmed but deeply conflicted and guilt-ridden about it. You could also have a cold dead fish with low scores in both: the Beast is relatively quiet but the guy's a Bastard anyway. The extremes are also possible.<br /> <br /> Frenzy rolls are straight-up contests between Humanity and the Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T17:38:28-07:00","id":1383058,"title":"","content":"If all you're doing is inverting the score, what does this actually do? Isn't it mechanically identical with a different label?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T19:21:17-07:00","id":1383071,"title":"","content":"I've considered something like this in the past. Maybe make it like Rage, only you spend it to increase strength, it can't be spent during the day, and 10 minus this rating is the maximum dice you can roll during the day.<br /> <br /> They eventually incorporated a somewhat similar idea into blood potence back in Requiem, so I'd long since abandoned this idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T09:36:09-07:00","id":1383149,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24641-sarcasticjazzhands\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24641\" data-vbnamecard=\"24641\">SarcasticJazzHands</a> <br /> <br /> How would you handle this at chagen? Do all pcs begin with the same &quot;Beast rating&quot;? Do they pay for having a different initial rating, such as if they are building a serial killer versus a naive nun?<br /> <br /> How does one lower their permanent Beast rating... is there an xp cost, like how you can raise Humanity?<br /> <br /> Also, I am unclear on how your mechanic makes Paths easier to integrate. It changes the bookkeeping some, but I don't see any differences in the sort of behavior that is penalized or encouraged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T15:39:11-07:00","id":1383234,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25972_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25972\" data-vbnamecard=\"25972\">IllithidActivity</a> - Simple, labels matter. Much of the debate about Paths in V5 stems from the use of Humanity as the base descriptor. But, as has been pointed out before, Humanity was used in all previous verions, until the Path system came out and then there was an alternate system made.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13136\" data-vbnamecard=\"13136\">Legendre</a> - That is an interesting system. How do they each raise/lower?<br /> \u200b<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3598_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3598\" data-vbnamecard=\"3598\">CajunKhan</a> - Rage is already used in Werewolf, and would be too confusing with cross over items.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11558_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11558\" data-vbnamecard=\"11558\">Nosimplehiway</a> - I imagine everyone would begin with Beast of 3 ( since you start with a Humanity of 7) And then that is modified further by your various Predator Types as needed. Because of the Beast is tied into being a Vampire and not something that carried over from being a human, those two wouldn't have to start with different Beast ratings. Another option would be that Humanity is a rating that humans/ghouls have, and they then begin their unlife with 10 - their Humanity rating as their beginning Beast. <br /> Yes, there would be an EXP cost to lower your beast rating, but not quite sure how to do the calculation yet, since with Humanity, it takes more EXP to increase humanity at higher levels, it should also cost more EXP to keep the beast rating low at the lower levels.<br /> As I said before, labels matter. The reason many Paths came into being was as methods of keeping the Beast at bay while emphasizing a part of that vampires particular pedigree (Blood, Metamorphosis, Night and others). I agree with much of the talk of Touchstones needing a revamping, to allow for non-human, or at least non-specific persons. I always drop back to Julian Luna from Kindred the Embraced TV show. He had his wife's grave as a touchstone, and would go to it and earthmeld there every time he was in the area. His mortal family as a whole was a touchstone, as he kept tabs on them all, but would focus on one or two for a while. In the show, after the funeral of his descendant, he latched onto a different family member, until she was embraced by a rival clan, which greatly affected him, as I am sure it would have mechanically via touchstones.<br /> I think looking at Convictions and Tenets as &quot;Ways to keep the Beast at bay&quot; and not &quot;Ways to maintain Humanity&quot; it can be easy to have a Path focused game. I like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24788-chipotlechris\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24788_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24788\" data-vbnamecard=\"24788\">chipotlechris</a> and his write up of his modifications of touchstones and Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24641-sarcasticjazzhands","name":"SarcasticJazzHands","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T16:10:03-07:00","id":1383241,"title":"","content":"LIKE rage. Demon chi is also LIKE rage, without actually being rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T17:16:57-07:00","id":1383244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382975-humanity-variant-the-beast?p=1383241#post1383241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">LIKE rage. Demon chi is also LIKE rage, without actually being rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Angst and Torment might be better comparison points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{