with cross over items.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11558_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11558\" data-vbnamecard=\"11558\">Nosimplehiway</a> - I imagine everyone would begin with Beast of 3 ( since you start with a Humanity of 7) And then that is modified further by your various Predator Types as needed. Because of the Beast is tied into being a Vampire and not something that carried over from being a human, those two wouldn't have to start with different Beast ratings. Another option would be that Humanity is a rating that humans/ghouls have, and they then begin their unlife with 10 - their Humanity rating as their beginning Beast.<br /> Yes, there would be an EXP cost to lower your beast rating, but not quite sure how to do the calculation yet, since with Humanity, it takes more EXP to increase humanity at higher levels, it should also cost more EXP to keep the beast rating low at the lower levels.<br /> As I said before, labels matter. The reason many Paths came into being was as methods of keeping the Beast at bay while emphasizing a part of that vampires particular pedigree (Blood, Metamorphosis, Night and others). I agree with much of the talk of Touchstones needing a revamping, to allow for non-human, or at least non-specific persons. I always drop back to Julian Luna from Kindred the Embraced TV show. He had his wife's grave as a touchstone, and would go to it and earthmeld there every time he was in the area. His mortal family as a whole was a touchstone, as he kept tabs on them all, but would focus on one or two for a while. In the show, after the funeral of his descendant, he latched onto a different family member, until she was embraced by a rival clan, which greatly affected him, as I am sure it would have mechanically via touchstones.<br /> I think looking at Convictions and Tenets as &quot;Ways to keep the Beast at bay&quot; and not &quot;Ways to maintain Humanity&quot; it can be easy to have a Path focused game. I like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24788-chipotlechris\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24788_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24788\" data-vbnamecard=\"24788\">chipotlechris</a> and his write up of his modifications of touchstones and Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Non-Confrontational Question: If they changed the label from Humanity to Paths/Road but kept the mechanics all the same, you would be fine with it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T01:16:30-07:00","id":1383304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SarcasticJazzHands</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382975-humanity-variant-the-beast?p=1383234#post1383234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13136\" data-vbnamecard=\"13136\">Legendre</a> - That is an interesting system. How do they each raise/lower?</div> </div> </div> </div>Humanity is raised, and Beast is lowered, by spending XP. It's the only way and it's expensive.<br /> <br /> Humanity is lost the usual way: through the performance of immoral acts and omissions. The system is very, very customized and doesn't resemble VtM RAW at all. There are things called &quot;Inhumanity Traits&quot; which function as a sort of categorical immunity to moral degeneration. The gist is that if you commit an act that registers for your Humanity score and don't have immunity for that sort of act, then you check to see if you lose humanity by contesting your Humanity against the number of Inhumanities you have. If you lose, you lose a point of Humanity. <br /> <br /> Beast -- which starts at 3 -- is gained a few ways. The first is committing immoral acts/omissions <b><i>while in frenzy</i></b>. If you undergo moral degeneration while in frenzy, you gain beast instead of losing humanity. You can also gain Beast by voluntarily frenzying, or by failing to attempt to resist a frenzy. You can also gain a Beast Point by using up all of your &quot;rerolls&quot; during a combat. (One of the additional rules is that when you are in Frenzy, you can reroll a number of combat or physical contests equal to your Beast Rating.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T22:21:04-07:00","id":1383511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382975-humanity-variant-the-beast?p=1383257#post1383257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Non-Confrontational Question: If they changed the label from Humanity to Paths/Road but kept the mechanics all the same, you would be fine with it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Me personally? Yes. I would have no issue with the actual label for it. I am throwing this out there as something that would be acceptable to the whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24641-sarcasticjazzhands","name":"SarcasticJazzHands","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T08:51:55-07:00","id":1392212,"title":"","content":"So, a few other thoughts I've gotten while kicking this around.<br /> <br /> A vampire's Predator Type is tied with their Beast rating. A vampire finds a particular way of feeding that seems to keep the Beast docile and happy within. This is reflected in the mechanical benefits bestowed by the Predator Type. When a vampire feeds in ways that do not match with their PT, they would incur &quot;stains&quot; against the Beast (I am thinking of calling these Ravages). This can change the mindset of picking a PT, though I know of course it can lead to &quot;We are all going to go Consensualist and feed every morning from my Herd.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24641-sarcasticjazzhands","name":"SarcasticJazzHands","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T09:53:52-07:00","id":1392230,"title":"","content":"On the one hand, it\u2019s fine. On the other hand, I don\u2019t see what it would accomplish that the Humanity system doesn\u2019t already.<br /> <br /> I think people get caught up in the terminology of previous editions, in which paths were presented as antonymous with humanity. In V5 \u201cHumanity\u201d is how much you\u2019re a rational, thinking being and not a mindless wight, so it includes all the various philosophies presented by the paths in previous editions, as well as their purpose. Its no longer tied to a specific Hierarchy of Sins, and you\u2019re free to pick your Convictions. I expect all that\u2019s needed is a minor adjustment to how Touchstones work, and the current system already has you there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T10:20:15-07:00","id":1392235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382975-humanity-variant-the-beast?p=1392230#post1392230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think people get caught up in the terminology of previous editions...</div> </div> </div> </div>That is why I thought to present this option.<br /> <br /> So, more put together elevator pitch for it:<br /> <br /> Beast is a rating of the strength of your inner predator. When you do predatory things, things that empower the Beast, it can grow. When you connect with humans and Humanity, the Beast can shrink back. When you do Predatory acts, if they are inline with Chronicle Tenets and personal Convictions, you can lessen the Ravages of the Beast. If you choose to take Touchstones (which should be treated differently with this system) they are points of contact, interaction systems to keep the Beast at bay. Touchstones, therefore, can then be people, as well as places, items or even routines, things that connect and remind you of when you didn't have the Beast.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24641-sarcasticjazzhands","name":"SarcasticJazzHands","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T10:55:21-07:00","id":1392250,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. And also to be fair, the paths were originally just reskinned Humanity, with reskinned virtues, so it\u2019s not out of keeping with tradition. <br /> <br /> Requiem did something similar with an optional rule wherein instead of Humanity decreasing, Atrocity would increase (only it would also add dice to your pools, sort of like if hunger in V5 added instead of swapped dice).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}